<title>HONG KONG: MUI Hong Kong 1996 net loss HK$9.06 mln.</title>
<headline>MUI Hong Kong 1996 net loss HK$9.06 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.6 loss  vs 1.3 gain (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	 vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  3.93 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    9.06 loss vs 7.01 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,129.76  vs 866.23</p>
<p>    Company name		 MUI Hong Kong Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - MUI Hong Kong, formerly Morning Star Holdings Ltd, provides travel and related services.</p>
<p>The calculation of loss per share is based on the weighted average of 578.50 million shares vs 542.31 million shares after adjusting for the effect of the two-for-one rights issue in November 1996. Comparative share earnings has been adjusted accordingly.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on the write down of fixed assets and provision for non-recoverable deposits associated with the group's planned relocation of its headquarters.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs two H.K. cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
